['Replace an informal idiom with neutral business English.','We are just kicking the can down the road.','We are merely postponing the problem|We are just postponing the problem|We are only delaying the problem|We are simply postponing the problem','A neutral paraphrase preserves the criticism without the conversational idiom.'],
['Avoid overclaiming. Use suggests an association.','This small observational study proves causation.','This small observational study suggests an association|The study suggests an association','Suggests an association calibrates the claim to limited observational evidence.'],
['Remove the empty wording while preserving the time reference.','At this point in time we are unable to proceed.','We are currently unable to proceed|We cannot proceed now|At present we are unable to proceed|We are unable to proceed now','Currently or now replaces a wordy time expression without changing the meaning.']
